# Git does NOT read .dockerignore. Everything excluded there for secrecy
# reasons has to be repeated here, or publishing this repo leaks it.
#
# Note: keep the comments in this file generic. An exclusion list that explains
# internal hostnames and key paths in detail leaks them just as effectively as
# committing the files would.

# ---- credentials: never, under any circumstances ----
.gh
.f
.k
.atkey
.flytoken
.admintoken
.env
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
id_ed25519*
.flyapp

# Per-use credential fetches land in dot-prefixed files at the repo root. The
# named entries above are the ones that have existed; this catch-all covers any
# future one, because a credential that is merely untracked is one `git add -A`
# away from being public.
.gh*
.cf_*
.cr_*
.*token*
.*secret*

# ---- private key-manager client helpers ----
# Operational tooling for a private stack, not part of the app.
src/cr_*.mjs

# ---- private deployment stack ----
# Reverse-proxy, SSO and internal hostnames for the self-hosted instance.
deploy/

# ---- internal working notes ----
# Project memory: internal addresses, host access recipes, decision log.
# Working notes, not public documentation.
MEMORY.md
DECISIONS.md
STATE.md

# ---- security audit ----
# Documents findings that are not yet all fixed on the live deployment.
# Publishing it would amount to an exploit guide. Re-include once closed.
docs/SECURITY_AUDIT.md

# ---- build artefacts and local data ----
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
output/
_*.db
_*.html

# ---- databases and host-specific deploy files ----
# Feedback databases carry real user submissions. The pre-audit schema also
# held a reporter name and third-party case references, so an archived copy
# is personal data even though the live schema no longer collects it.
# The earlier `_*.db` rule only caught underscore-prefixed names.
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
archive/

# Compose files for private hosts: internal addresses, VLAN layout and the
# access assumptions of a specific machine. The app does not need them.
# Per-host compose overrides may carry site addressing; ignore by default and
# allow-list the ones deliberately sanitised for publication.
compose.*.yaml
!compose.yaml
# Tracked on purpose: the pull deployer resets the working tree to origin/main,
# so the self-hosted compose file must be reproducible from the repo. It holds
# no secrets -- the AT key lives in .env (ignored below).
!compose.selfhosted.yaml

# ---- throwaway probe and screenshot scripts ----
# Investigation tooling; keep the repo to the actual application.
#
# EXCEPT shot_px.py and shot_ui4.py (un-ignored below): those two stopped
# being throwaway the moment CI started running them as the render gate.
# They are the only check that proves the page actually DREW -- generated
# HTML/CSS is valid markup even when it styles nothing, so nothing throws and
# nothing logs. A gate that is not in the repo cannot run on a clean checkout.
src/probe*.py
src/shot*.py
!src/shot_px.py
!src/shot_ui4.py
src/seed_feedback.py

# Licensed third-party art — "Train Station Tileset" by Pixels On Ultra.
# The licence permits use and editing but FORBIDS redistribution ("edited or
# not") and explicitly says to keep the assets out of a public repository when
# the project is open source. This repo is public. These paths are belt-and-
# braces alongside the broader output/ rule above, which must not be narrowed
# without re-checking this.
output/tileset_peek/
web/tileset/
assets/tileset/
Train_Station_Tileset*/
*Train_Station_Tileset*.zip
